msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/opportunities/pro/class-subscription-multiplier-opportunity.php:51
msgid "Setting a value in the Subscription Multiplier field will multiply the conversion value of subscription products by the specified value to better match the lifetime value of the subscription. This will improve campaign optimization."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/opportunities/pro/class-tiktok-advanced-matching-opportunity.php:37
msgid "TikTok Advanced Matching"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/opportunities/pro/class-tiktok-advanced-matching-opportunity.php:42
msgid "TikTok Pixel is enabled but Advanced Matching is not active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/opportunities/pro/class-tiktok-advanced-matching-opportunity.php:46
msgid "Advanced Matching sends hashed customer data (e.g. email) to TikTok, improving conversion attribution and audience matching, especially when cookies are blocked or users switch devices."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/opportunities/pro/class-tiktok-eapi-opportunity.php:37
msgid "TikTok Events API"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/opportunities/pro/class-tiktok-eapi-opportunity.php:42
msgid "TikTok Pixel is enabled but the Events API is not configured."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/opportunities/pro/class-tiktok-eapi-opportunity.php:46
msgid "The Events API sends events directly from your server to TikTok, bypassing browser limitations like ad blockers and cookie restrictions. This improves attribution accuracy and campaign optimization."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:110
msgid "List Settings Backups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:111
msgid "Lists the automatic settings backups of Pixel Manager for WooCommerce, newest first. Every settings save creates one. Use the timestamp with pmw/get-settings-backup to inspect a backup and with pmw/restore-settings-backup to roll back. The backup marked active is the state in use and cannot be restored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:125
msgid "Get Settings Backup"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:126
msgid "Returns the settings tree stored in one automatic backup, to compare it with the current settings (pmw/export-settings) before restoring. Secrets such as API tokens are replaced by null and listed in redacted_paths. Call pmw/list-settings-backups first for the timestamps."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:142
msgid "Export Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:143
msgid "Returns the complete current settings tree, including internal keys that pmw/get-settings does not list, like the settings export in the admin. Secrets such as API tokens are replaced by null and listed in redacted_paths, so the export cannot restore those secrets. Use pmw/get-settings to read individual settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:155
msgid "Restore Settings Backup"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:156
msgid "Replaces all current settings with an automatic backup, like the Restore button on the Support page. Refused for the currently active backup and for a backup that fails validation. The settings in use before the restore stay available as their own backup, so a restore is undone by restoring that one. Confirm with the user first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:176
msgid "Import Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:177
msgid "Replaces all settings with a complete settings tree, like the settings import on the Support page. Use it only with a settings file the user provided. Every field runs its validator, unknown keys are dropped, and an invalid tree is refused with the failing paths. A backup of the previous settings is created first. To change individual settings use pmw/update-settings instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:212
msgid "Get Payment Gateway Accuracy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:213
msgid "Returns the daily tracking accuracy per payment gateway, the data behind the chart on the Diagnostics page: for each day and gateway the number of orders, how many of them the browser measured, how many Automatic Conversion Recovery recovered, and how many were excluded for missing consent. Low measured shares point at gateways that skip the order confirmation page. Without dates it covers the last 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:245
msgid "Get Logs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:246
msgid "Returns the Pixel Manager log files, the same files the log download on the Support page zips. Only the plugin's own log sources (starting with pmw) can be read. Each file is returned from its end, capped at max_bytes, which is where the newest entries are. Logs only fill while the logger is enabled (general.logger.* settings) and WooCommerce file logging is on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:275
msgid "Get First Event Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:276
msgid "Returns whether the storefront already confirmed that the pixels load (pixelsLive, set by the first visit after setup) and whether the first order was tracked (firstOrder), the status strip on the Dashboard. beaconPending true means no storefront visit has confirmed the setup yet; ask the user to open the shop once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:306
msgid "List Opportunities"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:307
msgid "Lists the optimization opportunities the Opportunities page shows for this shop, sorted by impact (high first): features that would improve tracking quality or ad performance, with a description, setup and documentation links and whether the user dismissed the card. Most are resolved by changing settings with pmw/update-settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:337
msgid "Dismiss Opportunity"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:338
msgid "Dismisses an opportunity card, as the Dismiss button on the Opportunities page does. It only hides the card and changes no setting. Undo with pmw/restore-opportunity."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:352
msgid "Restore Opportunity"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:353
msgid "Shows a dismissed opportunity card again, as Restore on the Opportunities page does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:367
msgid "Get Admin Notices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:368
msgid "Returns the state of the notices and cards the admin shows the user besides opportunities: the onboarding checklist, the one-time server load warning, the first-event confirmation, the rating request, the trial promotion and SweetCode Cloud delivery problems (failed destinations, exhausted quota). Use pmw/acknowledge-notice to answer one the way the user would in the admin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:400
msgid "Acknowledge Notice"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:401
msgid "Answers an admin notice or card the way the user would in the admin. type and id: generic-notification with the notification id (for example trial-promotion) or dismiss_notification with a Classic notification id dismiss it; onboarding with dismiss hides the checklist, with consent, diagnostics, pixie or pro marks that step done; first_event with dismiss-celebration hides the first order celebration; server_load_warning with capi acknowledges the server load warning; rating with rating_done or later answers the rating request. Only do this when the user asked for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:442
msgid "Get LTV Recalculation Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:443
msgid "Returns whether a lifetime value recalculation over the order history is running or scheduled. The lifetime value calculation requires an active Pro license; without one the call is refused with that reason."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:452
msgid "Run LTV Recalculation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:453
msgid "Recalculates the customer lifetime value of the whole order history through the Action Scheduler, like the recalculation control on the General page. mode run starts now, mode schedule queues it for the next quiet moment. It walks every order and loads the server for a while on large shops, so confirm with the user first. Requires an active Pro license and a recent Action Scheduler; refused with the reason otherwise. Stop with pmw/stop-ltv-recalculation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:469
msgid "Stop LTV Recalculation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:470
msgid "Cancels a running or scheduled lifetime value recalculation. Values already recalculated stay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:506
msgid "Get SweetCode Cloud Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:507
msgid "Returns the state of the SweetCode Cloud server-side proxy connection shown on the Server-Side page: whether it is connected and active, the proxy hostname, the last configuration sync and its error, plan, usage and quota, and destinations that are failing. Call this first before changing anything about SweetCode Cloud. The sync token is never returned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:522
msgid "Get SweetCode Cloud Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:523
msgid "Returns the SweetCode Cloud diagnostic report for support: structured fields plus the same content as text. Tokens are redacted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:538
msgid "Test SweetCode Cloud Connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:539
msgid "Checks from the shop's server whether the SweetCode Cloud proxy hostname is reachable, like the connection test on the Server-Side page. success false with details means it is not reachable; the call itself does not fail then."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:555
msgid "Connect SweetCode Cloud"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:556
msgid "Connects the shop to SweetCode Cloud with the sync token from the SweetCode Cloud portal, like Activate on the Server-Side page: stores the token, registers the shop and pushes the tracking configuration. Refused when the token is missing or malformed, or when the portal rejects it (for example a token issued for another domain). Ask the user for the token; never guess one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:578
msgid "Sync SweetCode Cloud Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:579
msgid "Pushes the current tracking configuration to SweetCode Cloud now, like Sync on the Server-Side page. Settings changes are pushed automatically; use this after a failed sync (see last_sync_error in pmw/get-ssp-status)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:589
msgid "Enable or Disable SweetCode Cloud"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:590
msgid "Turns routing through SweetCode Cloud on or off while keeping the connection, like the toggle on the Server-Side page. Disabled, server-side events are sent from the shop directly again. Enabling is refused while no sync token is stored; connect first with pmw/connect-ssp."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:604
msgid "Update SweetCode Cloud Setting"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:605
msgid "Changes what happens to server-side events while SweetCode Cloud is unreachable: fallback_to_wc sends them from the shop directly, drop_events discards them. The same control as on the Server-Side page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:629
msgid "Disconnect SweetCode Cloud"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:630
msgid "Disconnects the shop from SweetCode Cloud, like Disconnect on the Server-Side page: deletes the sync token, proxy hostname and callback tokens and tells SweetCode Cloud. It cannot be undone; reconnecting needs the sync token from the portal again. To pause routing instead, use pmw/set-ssp-enabled with enabled false. Only do this when the user explicitly asked for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:652
msgid "Update GA4 Data API Credentials"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:653
msgid "Stores the Google service account key (the JSON file from Google Cloud) that lets the plugin read order attribution from the GA4 Data API, like the credentials upload in the GA4 settings. Every field is validated; an empty object removes the stored credentials. The private key is stored as a secret and never returned. Only use a key file the user provided."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:676
msgid "Get Order Attribution"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:677
msgid "Reads the GA4 attribution of one order (source, medium, campaign and the like) from the GA4 Data API, the table the order edit page shows. Requires GA4 Data API credentials (pmw/update-ga4-data-api-credentials). GA4 needs up to 48 hours before an order appears, so a recent order can return no rows. The result is the rendered table as HTML."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:746
msgid "Get Google Data Manager Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:747
msgid "Returns whether the Google Ads Data Manager conversion upload is active, the outcome of the last upload, and the browser-versus-upload summary shown on the Google card."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:763
msgid "Get Google Data Manager Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:764
msgid "Returns the Google Ads Data Manager diagnostics of the Diagnostics page: the conversion action in use, the daily identifier coverage for 30 days, the recent orders with the identifiers each side had, and a text report for support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:786
msgid "Test Google Data Manager Upload"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:787
msgid "Sends the latest order to the Google Ads Data Manager as a validate-only upload, like the test button on the Google card: Google checks authentication, account access, conversion action and payload without recording a conversion. Refused until the upload is configured."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:807
msgid "Get Google Data Manager Backfill Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:808
msgid "Returns the progress of the backfill that re-uploads orders whose Google Ads Data Manager upload failed: whether it is running, how many orders it scanned, how many failed uploads it found and recovered, and the last error it saw."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:838
msgid "Get Google Connection Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:839
msgid "Returns whether the shop is connected to a Google account through the SweetCode connection service, which Google account, and the state of each product: ga4, ads and datamanager are ready, scope_missing (the user declined that permission on Google's consent screen) or not_connected. needsReconnect true means the grant expired or was revoked. Call this first before any other Google connection ability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:848
msgid "Start Google Connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:849
msgid "Starts connecting a Google account and returns the Google consent page URL. Consent needs the user: hand redirectUrl to them to open in their browser and sign in; Google then sends them back to return_url. An agent cannot complete this step itself. Afterwards call pmw/get-google-connection-status. return_url must be on this site, for example the Pixel Manager admin page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:862
msgid "Disconnect Google"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:863
msgid "Disconnects the Google account: revokes the plugin's Google grant and turns off the Data Manager upload. The GA4 and Google Ads IDs in the settings stay, so browser tracking continues. Reconnecting needs the user to go through Google's consent again. Only do this when the user explicitly asked for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:873
msgid "List Google Ads Accounts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:874
msgid "Lists the Google Ads accounts the connected Google account can access. An account reached through a manager account carries loginCustomerId; pass it on to the other Google Ads abilities. Requires ads ready in pmw/get-google-connection-status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:888
msgid "List Google Ads Conversion Actions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:889
msgid "Lists the conversion actions of a Google Ads account, to pick the purchase conversion for pmw/connect-google-ads-conversion. By default only the actions that fit website purchase tracking are listed; all true lists every action."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:920
msgid "Connect Google Ads Conversion"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:921
msgid "Sets up Google Ads conversion tracking with a conversion action, the last step of the Google Ads wizard: either an existing action (conversion_action_id) or a new one created in the Google Ads account (create_name). It waits up to 20 seconds for Google to publish the conversion tag, then saves conversion ID and label and the Data Manager upload settings, as the wizard does. When Google has not published the tag in time the action exists already; call again later with its conversion_action_id. Creating an action changes the user's Google Ads account, so confirm the name with the user."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:946
msgid "Get Google Data Manager Permission"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:947
msgid "Returns whether the connected Google account granted the Data Manager permission the server-side conversion upload needs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:956
msgid "List GA4 Accounts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:957
msgid "Lists the Google Analytics accounts and their GA4 properties the connected Google account can access. Requires ga4 ready in pmw/get-google-connection-status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:971
msgid "Create GA4 Property"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:972
msgid "Creates a GA4 property in a Google Analytics account, with the shop's time zone and currency, as the GA4 wizard does. It changes the user's Google Analytics account, so confirm with the user first. A property with the same name is reused (existing true). Next, pmw/connect-ga4-stream."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1001
msgid "List GA4 Streams"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1002
msgid "Lists the web data streams of a GA4 property with their measurement IDs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1020
msgid "Connect GA4 Stream"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1021
msgid "Sets up GA4 tracking with a web data stream, the last step of the GA4 wizard: either an existing stream (stream_id) or a new one created in the property (create_name). Saves the stream's measurement ID as google.analytics.ga4.measurement_id. Creating a stream changes the user's GA4 property, so confirm with the user first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1056
msgid "Get Meta Connection Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1057
msgid "Returns whether the shop is connected to a Meta (Facebook) business account through the SweetCode connection service, and as whom. needsReconnect true means the grant expired or was revoked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1066
msgid "Start Meta Connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1067
msgid "Starts connecting a Meta business account and returns the Facebook Login for Business URL. Hand redirectUrl to the user to open in their browser; an agent cannot complete the login. Afterwards call pmw/get-meta-connection-status. return_url must be on this site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1085
msgid "Disconnect Meta"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1086
msgid "Disconnects the Meta business account. The pixel ID in the settings stays. Reconnecting needs the user to log in again. Only do this when the user explicitly asked for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1096
msgid "List Meta Pixels"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1097
msgid "Lists the Meta pixels (datasets) the connected business account can use, with their ad accounts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1111
msgid "Connect Meta Pixel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities-admin.php:1112
msgid "Sets up Meta tracking with a pixel, the last step of the Meta wizard: verifies the pixel with Meta and saves it as facebook.pixel_id. For server-side events a Conversions API token is set separately (facebook.capi.token via pmw/update-settings)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:98
msgid "Tracking & Analytics"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:99
msgid "Abilities related to conversion tracking, analytics pixels, and marketing tag management."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:203
msgid "Get Tracking Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:204
msgid "Retrieves the status of all configured tracking pixels in Pixel Manager for WooCommerce, including which pixels are active, their categories (marketing, statistics, optimization), and whether they use browser-side or server-side tracking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:341
msgid "Get Plugin Info"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:342
msgid "Retrieves general information about the Pixel Manager for WooCommerce plugin, including version, license tier (free/pro), distribution channel, and environment compatibility status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:407
msgid "Get Debug Info"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:408
msgid "Retrieves the full Pixel Manager for WooCommerce debug information report, including system environment details, active pixel configurations, consent mode settings, and tracking accuracy data. Useful for troubleshooting and support."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:485
msgid "Get Settings Schema"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:486
msgid "Retrieves the machine-readable catalog of all configurable Pixel Manager for WooCommerce settings, grouped by tracking destination (pixel) and plugin area. Each setting includes its dot-notation path, type, description (including where to find the value), default, whether it is required to activate the pixel, whether it is an advanced feature and what its benefit is, whether it requires the Pro version, and whether it is a secret. Settings that belong to the Pro version are always listed, but on a site without an active Pro license they are marked writable false and pmw/update-settings refuses them. Use this before reading or updating settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:560
msgid "Get Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:561
msgid "Retrieves the current values of all configurable Pixel Manager for WooCommerce settings. Secret values such as API tokens are never returned; for those only a set/not-set flag is included. Use pmw/get-settings-schema first to understand what each setting does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:616
msgid "Get Setup Status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:617
msgid "Retrieves a setup checklist for Pixel Manager for WooCommerce: which tracking pixels are configured and active, which required settings are missing, which advanced features are available but not enabled (including their benefits), and prioritized recommendations for the next setup step. Designed to drive guided setup conversations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:697
msgid "Update Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:698
msgid "Updates one or more Pixel Manager for WooCommerce settings by dot-notation path. Only the submitted settings are changed, all other settings are preserved. Each value is validated with the same rules as the admin UI (including format checks for IDs and tokens), and every save creates an automatic settings backup. A setting that belongs to the Pro version is refused with status forbidden on a site without an active Pro license, and nothing is written for it. Use pmw/get-settings-schema to discover the available paths, types and value formats."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:771
msgid "Configure Pixel"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-abilities.php:772
msgid "Configures a tracking pixel (destination) in Pixel Manager for WooCommerce in one call. Accepts the pixel key and a map of setting keys to values (e.g. for google_ads: conversion_id and conversion_label). Validates and saves the values, then returns the pixel's setup status: whether it is active, which required settings are still missing, and which advanced features are available with their benefits. Ideal for guided setup conversations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-logger.php:777
msgid "The Pixel Manager writes its log even though WooCommerce logging is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-logger.php:785
msgid "WooCommerce stores its log entries in the database, so the Pixel Manager entries are only visible under WooCommerce > Status > Logs, not through the \"View latest log\" and \"Download logs\" buttons."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the class name of WooCommerce's log handler
#: includes/class-logger.php:791
#, php-format
msgid "WooCommerce hands its log entries to %s instead of writing them to files, so the \"View latest log\" and \"Download logs\" buttons find no Pixel Manager entries."
msgstr ""

#: includes/pixels/class-pixel-manager.php:804
msgid "Too many requests"
msgstr ""

#: includes/pixels/class-pixel-manager.php:883
msgid "You can not view private data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/pixels/class-pixel-manager.php:1011
msgid "Try going through the setup process again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/pixels/class-pixel-manager.php:1917
msgid "Authentication required"
msgstr ""
